import boto3
import sagemaker
from sagemaker import get_execution_role


# Set custom bucket
bucket = 'insurance-prediction-bucket'  # Your custom S3 bucket
prefix = 'insurance-data'
role = get_execution_role()


# Local file to upload
local_file = 'insurance_pre.csv'


# Upload file to your specific bucket
session = sagemaker.Session()
s3_path = session.upload_data(path=local_file, bucket=bucket, key_prefix=prefix)


from utils import append_to_file
append_to_file("output.txt", "s3-path:", s3_path)


print(f"✅ File uploaded to your bucket at: {s3_path}")


========

| Code                                       | Explanation                                                                                    |
| ------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `import boto3`                             | Imports the AWS SDK for Python. It allows Python programs to interact with AWS services.       |
| `import sagemaker`                         | Imports the Amazon SageMaker Python SDK.                                                       |
| `from sagemaker import get_execution_role` | Imports the function used to get the IAM execution role assigned to the SageMaker environment. |
| `bucket = 'insurance-prediction-bucket'`   | Specifies the name of the destination S3 bucket where the file will be uploaded.               |
| `prefix = 'insurance-data'`                | Specifies the folder-like path inside the S3 bucket.                                           |
| `role = get_execution_role()`              | Gets the permissions/role used by SageMaker to access AWS resources.                           |
| `local_file = 'insurance_pre.csv'`         | Specifies the local CSV file that you want to upload.                                          |
| `session = sagemaker.Session()`            | Creates a SageMaker session to interact with SageMaker and related AWS services.               |
| `session.upload_data(...)`                 | Uploads the specified local file to the S3 bucket.                                             |
| `path=local_file`                          | Sends the file named `insurance_pre.csv`.                                                      |
| `bucket=bucket`                            | Uses the bucket name stored in the `bucket` variable.                                          |
| `key_prefix=prefix`                        | Places the uploaded file inside the `insurance-data` path in S3.                               |
| `s3_path = ...`                            | Stores the resulting S3 location of the uploaded file.                                         |
| `from utils import append_to_file`         | Imports a custom function named `append_to_file` from `utils.py`.                              |
| `append_to_file(...)`                      | Writes/appends the S3 path information into `output.txt`.                                      |
| `print(...)`                               | Displays a success message and the S3 location of the uploaded file.                           |


======

Example result

The file may be stored at a location similar to:

s3://insurance-prediction-bucket/insurance-data/insurance_pre.csv

This is useful because your Machine Learning training, preprocessing, processing jobs, or SageMaker models can later access the dataset directly from Amazon S3.

